From 1e303caedc93ec1589c42d6300ac6be2263c23e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:03:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] relay_metrics: Export HS descriptor POST outcome counters

Add tor_relay_hsdir_post_total{status,reason} on the MetricsPort to count HS descriptor POST outcomes by HTTP status and failure reason:

- status="200",reason="ok": descriptor accepted and stored in the HSDir cache (hs_cache_store_as_dir() > 0).

- status="400",reason="rev_counter": descriptor passed format, certificate, and signature validation, but had a revision_counter <= the cached entry (hs_cache_store_as_dir() == 0). Legitimate services (stock C Tor re-uploads, Onionbalance frontends, or active-active standby failover) can trigger this without indicating malformed traffic.

- status="400",reason="bad_url": POST path under /tor/hs/ had an unsupported version or a subpath other than /publish.

- status="400",reason="invalid_desc": descriptor failed size, outer layer parse, superencrypted layer parse, descriptor signing cert, or outer signature validation (hs_cache_store_as_dir() < 0).

Add unit tests in test_hs_cache.c covering all four outcome buckets.
